{
  "abstract": "Markman proved the Hodge conjecture for Weil classes on abelian sixfolds of split Weil type. A key step is that a secant sheaf on an abelian threefold has its equivariant Ext algebra generated by the image of Hochschild cohomology. We show that this mechanism has a numerical consequence in every dimension $g$. If $HH^*(X)$ maps onto $\\mathrm{Ext}^*(F,F)^G$, then this Ext algebra is the Gorenstein algebra attached to $\\mathrm{ch}(F)$, and $\\chi(F,F)/|G|$ equals its Euler characteristic $e(\\mathrm{ch}\\,F)$. For a class in a one-place secant plane, $e=-(1+(-1)^g)$, while $\\chi(F,F)$ has sign $(-1)^{g/2}$. So the mechanism is impossible on every abelian $g$-fold with $4\\mid g$, which includes the split Weil eightfolds over $\\mathbf Q$, and it forces $\\chi(F,F)=-2|G|$ when $g\\equiv2\\bmod4$. We extend this to the CM-type planes of Markman's real-multiplication setting for $g>4$. We also give explicit secant sheaves on genus-five and genus-six Jacobians over $\\mathbf Q(\\sqrt{-3})$. At genus six, on a very general Jacobian, the mechanism fails for every torsion-free sheaf and every complex of Markman's type of rank $\\pm1$, whatever the norm of the class, and for the minimal rank-zero classes. Finally, flat hyperholomorphic carriers are excluded by a positivity argument. The fourfold degree-2 consequences were obtained earlier in rStation papers 37 and 127, and we state precisely how the present results extend them.",
